        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Tarawa</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">20–23 November 1943; the landing was at 09:10 on 20 November and Betio was declared secure at 13:30 on 23 November</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Betio, the largest island of Tarawa Atoll in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilbert-islands">Gilbert Islands</a>, now part of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiribati">Kiribati</a> but then a Japanese-occupied British colony</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, under Admiral Raymond Spruance, Admiral Richmond Kelly Turner and Major General Julian C. Smith, with the 2nd Marine Division (roughly 12,000 Marines on Tarawa); <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, under Rear Admiral Keiji Shibazaki, with a garrison counted at 3,636 or at 4,500 defenders, besides about 1,200 Korean labourers</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">American victory: Betio was taken and almost the whole garrison killed, with 4,690 of the island's defenders dead and 3,166 casualties in the 2nd Marine Division.</span></div>
        </div>
